{%- comment -%}
  Head-level robots control for pages that must not be indexed by default.

  Why this lives in the head: a robots meta tag is only honoured inside
  <head>. A section renders in <body>, so a section-level robots tag is
  ignored by search engines. This snippet is rendered from
  layout/theme.liquid head, alongside the longeva schema snippets.

  Default-safe doorway-page guardrail (Brief v4 Section 12):
  the local-area town pages (Rochdale, Manchester, Oldham, Bury, Bolton,
  Blackburn, Salford, Near Me, Manchester Airport) are near-identical by
  nature. Google treats a single clinic spinning up many "travel clinic
  in [town]" pages as scaled/doorway content. So every page on the
  local-area template is noindex by default, purely from the template
  suffix (no per-page metafield needed to be safe).

  Opt a page IN to indexing only once it carries genuinely unique local
  content: set its page metafield custom.allow_index (boolean) to true.

  Service/vaccine PRODUCTS (page/product duplication clean-up):

  - VACCINE products (product.vaccine.json) always pair with a real
    indexable page in this theme's architecture (the vaccine hub /
    individual vaccine pages) — longeva-service-layout-product.liquid
    is a confirmed structural fork of longeva-service-layout.liquid,
    same H1/body/FAQ/CTA. Kept noindex by default here; follow is kept
    so Sesami's own scripts and any internal links stay fully
    crawlable — only indexing is blocked, nothing about booking.
    Genuine exceptions can opt back in via product metafield
    custom.allow_index (boolean) = true.

  - SERVICE products (product.service.json) are NOT blanket-noindexed.
    Checked directly in Shopify Admin (11 Sep 2026): active service
    products including Adrenaline Nasal Spray, Jet Lag Consultation
    and Thrush Treatment have NO dedicated SEO landing page at all —
    the product IS their only indexable surface, so noindexing them by
    template suffix would have silently removed valid, standalone
    services from organic search. Service products index by default;
    noindex only when a specific product is confirmed (by whoever
    manages the catalogue) to have an approved, published, dedicated
    page equivalent, flagged explicitly via product metafield
    custom.noindex (boolean) = true — the same opt-out convention
    already used for structural-shell pages above, applied per-product
    rather than guessed from the template suffix. custom.allow_index on
    a service product overrides custom.noindex back to indexable, for
    the same reason it overrides the local-area/vaccine defaults.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign noindex = false

  comment
    Local-area town pages: noindex by default (template), opt IN via
    custom.allow_index. See above.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'local-area'
    assign noindex = true
    if page.metafields.custom.allow_index.value == true
      assign noindex = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Structural shells (Brief v4): a page is created published so navigation
    resolves and the structure is testable, but carries custom.noindex = true
    until its content lands, so an empty page is never indexed. Clear the
    metafield (or set it false) once Alicia or Varsha have filled the page.
  endcomment
  if page.metafields.custom.noindex.value == true
    assign noindex = true
  endif

  comment
    Vaccine booking products: noindex by default (template), opt IN via
    product metafield custom.allow_index. See above.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'vaccine'
    assign noindex = true
    if product.metafields.custom.allow_index.value == true
      assign noindex = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Service booking products: indexable by default (many have no page
    equivalent at all). noindex only when explicitly flagged per-product
    via custom.noindex once a page equivalent is confirmed; allow_index
    always wins if both are set. See above.
  endcomment
  if template.suffix == 'service'
    if product.metafields.custom.noindex.value == true
      assign noindex = true
    endif
    if product.metafields.custom.allow_index.value == true
      assign noindex = false
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if noindex -%}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- endif -%}
